  "fieldGuide": [
    {
      "question": "Is Karnali the same as Province No. 6?",
      "answer": "Yes. The provincial assembly selected the Karnali name and Birendranagar capital on 12 Falgun 2074, corresponding to 24 February 2018. The province includes ten districts.",
      "source": "https://edd.karnali.gov.np/sites/edd/files/2025-08/%E0%A4%B6%E0%A5%88%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%B7%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%95%20%E0%A4%AA%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%8B%E0%A4%AB%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%87%E0%A4%B2%20%E0%A4%86.%E0%A4%B5.%20%E0%A5%A8%E0%A5%A6%E0%A5%AE%E0%A5%A7-%E0%A5%AE%E0%A5%A8.pdf"
    },
    {
      "question": "Where should I begin?",
      "answer": "Birendranagar works well for a Surkhet-based introduction and Dailekh road touring. Nepalgunj, in neighbouring Lumbini, is a useful positioning gateway for some mountain flights. Confirm the actual connection rather than treating a gateway as a guaranteed service.",
      "source": "https://ntb.gov.np/rara-national-park"
    },
    {
      "question": "Can I visit Rara and Phoksundo in one short trip?",
      "answer": "They have different approaches and logistical demands. Plan one well-supported journey at a time unless a specialist operator has designed a longer itinerary with realistic transfers, altitude preparation and buffers.",
      "source": "https://ntb.gov.np/shey-phoksundo-national-park"
    },
    {
      "question": "Are the high lakes easy because I can fly nearby?",
      "answer": "A flight does not remove altitude or remoteness. Have an appropriate arrival, ascent and overnight plan, suitable insurance and a way to obtain help. Seek pre-travel medical advice for your own health needs.",
      "source": "https://ntb.gov.np/en/plan-your-trip/before-you-come/safety-in-the-mountains"
    },
    {
      "question": "Do I need trekking permits?",
      "answer": "Requirements depend on nationality and the exact route. Parts of Dolpo, Humla and Mugu are restricted areas, and park entry is a separate matter. Confirm the latest requirements with the Department of Immigration and a registered trekking agency before departure.",
      "source": "https://immigration.gov.np/trekking-permit"
    },
    {
      "question": "When is the best time to come?",
      "answer": "There is no single season for the whole province. Mild, dry weather often suits valley and heritage touring; northern routes depend on snow, passes, flights and local support. Check your particular route rather than relying on a province-wide promise.",
      "source": "https://ntb.gov.np/en/karnali-province"
    },
    {
      "question": "Can I rely on fixed road or flight times?",
      "answer": "No. Build flexible connections and confirm roads, vehicles, flight operation and overnight stops locally. Carry a plan for delays and avoid booking a tight international departure immediately after a mountain return.",
      "source": "https://ntb.gov.np/latest-travel-updates"
    },
    {
      "question": "Are all heritage sites open?",
      "answer": "Do not assume so. Religious rules, maintenance and earthquake damage can affect access. Jajarkot’s historic structures in particular require current local confirmation; photographs may show earlier conditions.",
      "source": "https://hellocm.karnali.gov.np/grievance-track/07-2024-9XYZ5F"
    },
    {
      "question": "How should I approach village and monastery visits?",
      "answer": "Use local hosts or guides, ask before entering or photographing, and follow each community’s customs. Pay fairly for time and services, and avoid giving gifts directly to children.",
      "source": "https://whc.unesco.org/document/1098"
    },
    {
      "question": "What do the route and budget tools include?",
      "answer": "They organize your ideas, dates, saved places and your own cost estimates. They do not reserve transport, obtain permits or verify live prices. The Rara outline includes positioning days outside Karnali and must be adapted by an operator.",
      "source": "https://ntb.gov.np/rara-national-park"
    }
  ],
